       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Each 1,700 mg dose also exceeds the usual maximum single dose of about 850 mg to 1,000 mg. At this dose the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis goes up substantially.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** This could be 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Something else.** If so, please give me the dose and frequency.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'll then enter it with a note that the dose was verified by the attending."
